# Maximum cybersecurity (Medora)

**Priority:** Security to the max is a product requirement for a healthcare EMR. This is **defense in depth** and PHI-aware engineering; it is not a compliance certification checklist.

## Architecture boundary

- UI → mirrored API → `$lib/server/**` only ([`remote-api-pages-flow.mdc`](remote-api-pages-flow.mdc)).
- **Never** import `$lib/server/**` in `.svelte` or client modules; enforced by [`check-ui-boundary.mjs`](scripts/check-ui-boundary.mjs).
- **Never** ship secrets in client bundles; no `$env/static/private` or `$app/env/private` in UI ([`check-security-markup.mjs`](scripts/check-security-markup.mjs)).

## Authentication and session

- Better Auth via [`hooks.server.ts`](src/hooks.server.ts); session on `event.locals`; fail closed on auth errors.
- Mutating Medora APIs: [`rejectMutatingMedoraApiWithoutTwoFactor`](src/lib/server/medora/auth/require-two-factor-for-mutation.server.ts) for enrolled staff roles.
- Session cookies: HttpOnly, Secure in production, SameSite appropriate (Better Auth config).

## Authorization (every API and sensitive load)

Order of checks:

1. Authenticate (`401` if no user).
2. Resolve role (`event.locals.userRoleId`, admin permissions when applicable).
3. **Hospital scope:** validate `hospital_id` route param against `event.locals.allowedHospitalIds` / staff hospitals; never trust client id alone ([`hospital.server.ts`](src/lib/server/medora/hospital.server.ts) patterns).
4. Page/feature permission for admin-team actions.

Use generic **403/404** messages; avoid user/hospital enumeration via error text.

## Input and output

- Validate request bodies and query params at API boundary (Zod or project schema).
- Database access via Drizzle only (parameterized); no string-concatenated SQL.
- API list DTOs: **minimum necessary** PHI; no fat audit blobs in every row.
- User-visible errors: [`sanitizeUserFacingErrorText`](src/lib/util/user-facing-error.util.ts) / toast sanitizers (no stacks, SQL, HTML dumps).

## XSS and `{@html}`

Allowed without extra review (allowlist in `check-security-markup`):

- [`SeoHead.svelte`](src/lib/component/own/snippet/seo/SeoHead.svelte) JSON-LD via [`serializeJsonLd`](src/lib/util/seo.util.ts).
- [`DocsArticle.svelte`](src/lib/component/own/global/public/docs/DocsArticle.svelte) trusted docs pipeline HTML.
- [`MariRichEditorPreview.svelte`](src/lib/component/own/library/mari/text-editor/rich-editor/MariRichEditorPreview.svelte) for sanitized stored content only.

**Ban** new `{@html}` for raw user/API/DB strings without security review and server-side sanitization on persist (TinyMCE skill).

## Open redirects

- Use [`sanitizeRedirectTo`](src/lib/util/two-factor-gate.util.ts): relative paths only, no `//`, no `http:`/`https:` off-site.
- Do not duplicate weaker redirect parsers in auth UI; import shared helper when touching those files.

## HTTP security headers

Applied centrally via [`security-headers.server.ts`](src/lib/server/http/security-headers.server.ts) in [`hooks.server.ts`](src/hooks.server.ts):

- `Content-Security-Policy` (pragmatic for SvelteKit inline boot scripts in [`app.html`](src/app.html))
- `Strict-Transport-Security` (HTTPS production)
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
- `X-Frame-Options` / `frame-ancestors`
- `Referrer-Policy`, `Permissions-Policy`
- `Cache-Control: no-store` on `/medora/**` and `/api/**` responses

Tune CSP forward when adding CDNs or third-party scripts; do not remove CSP to "fix" warnings.

## Logging and errors

- [`handleError`](src/hooks.server.ts): log URL, status, message; **no** passwords, tokens, session ids, or PHI payloads.
- Client console: do not log full API error bodies containing PHI.

## Secrets and dependencies

- Real credentials only in local `.env`; [`.env.example`](.env.example) placeholders only.
- Review high/critical `npm audit` findings before release; prefer patch upgrades for auth/crypto deps.

## Clinical and PHI handling

- Avoid PHI in query strings and analytics events where possible.
- Use domain audit hooks where they exist (e.g. lab audit) for sensitive workflow changes.
- **File uploads:** validate type/size; store outside public web root; authorize every download URL.
- Document templates and generated PDFs: hospital policy and consent flows apply.

## Finish checklist (new endpoint or form)

- [ ] Mirrored API with auth + hospital scope + permission checks
- [ ] Zod (or equivalent) validation on input
- [ ] Lean response DTO in `$lib/model/type/**`
- [ ] Sanitized user-facing errors
- [ ] No new `{@html}` without allowlist update and sanitization story
- [ ] 2FA gate respected for mutating Medora APIs when role requires it
- [ ] Security headers present on responses (hooks wrapper)

## Do not

- Trust `hospital_id` from the client without server-side membership check
- Return stack traces or SQL to the browser
- Log session tokens or patient identifiers in plain text
- Add `{@html}` for convenience on table cell or API string fields
- Disable security headers or CSP globally instead of narrowing directives
